repo:cloud#2 · os-warren · session_01JQwxbWTyRFQwYN1hZXbCHL

Filing gate: ② a class (a) out-of-scope finding from a cloud card's os-dev-report: cloud#4079 report 6735520788, F1. The cloud half is PR objectstack-ai/cloud#4087 (cloud#3825 item 4, answer transparency).

Dedupe: objectstack#31865 is the chatbot thumbs rating and turn ids, a different control. No open issue names a tool-result source renderer or answer transparency in plugin-chatbot.

Suggested grade: p3. Reader: a `domain:ui` seat.

## Problem

After objectstack-ai/cloud#4087, every Ask data tool (`query_records`, `query_data`, `get_record`, `aggregate_data`, `visualize_data`) returns a structured `source` block. It carries `object`, `label`, `filter`, `scope`, `groupBy`, `aggregations`, `orderBy`, `limit`, `records` and `line`.

A member cannot see it. `ui/packages/plugin-chatbot/src/ChatbotEnhanced.tsx:3201` sets `showPayload = processVisibility === 'debug' || (isAwaitingApproval && ...)`, so outside debug the tool JSON is not rendered. The only renderer, `SmartToolOutput` (`:3294`), prints raw JSON. A member sees the source only when the model copies `source.line` into its text. Reach: read from the renderer at framework pin `9e1f1f90`, not exercised in a live browser.

## What done looks like

1. A tool card that has a `source` object renders it for members, collapsed by default, labelled "How this was computed" (copy in all four locales):
   - object label;
   - filter;
   - grouping;
   - aggregations;
   - records, when present;
   - "only records visible to you" for `scope: visible_to_you`.
2. Only the `source` block is shown, never the rest of the tool payload; the debug surface is unchanged.
3. A result with no `source` renders as today.
4. Tests:
   - a card with `source` renders the block collapsed;
   - expanding it shows each part;
   - a card without `source` is unchanged;
   - non-debug visibility never shows the rest of the payload.

Seam: cloud `service-ai` ToolResult.source → plugin-chatbot tool card. Out of scope: a link to a filtered list (separate finding F2).
